/* 
    Padding, Margin, Border
   - Content ke andar jo space hota hai → Padding
   - Content + Padding ke bahar jo line hoti hai → Border
   - Border ke bahar jo space hoti hai → Margin
   - Matlab order: Content → Padding → Border → Margin
*/

/* 
    height: 400;
   - Is element ki height 400px ho jaayegi.
*/

/* 
    box-sizing: border-box;
   - By default height/width sirf content ke liye apply hoti hai (padding & border add hote hain upar se).
   - Lekin border-box karne par height/width ke andar hi content + padding + border adjust ho jaate hain.
   - Margin include nahi hota, kyunki margin element ke bahar hota hai.
*/

/* 
    Margin Collapse
   - Jab do elements ke margins ek dusre ko touch karte hain (top/bottom), 
     to dono add nahi hote. 
   - Sirf bada margin value apply hota hai.
*/

/* 
    font-family
   - Tum multiple fonts list kar sakte ho.
   - Browser left to right check karta hai.
   - Jo font available hoti hai, wahi apply ho jaati hai.
   - Example: font-family: "Roboto", "Arial", sans-serif;
*/

/* 
    Google Fonts Import
   Way 1: CSS file ke top me @import statement likhkar.
   Way 2: <link> tag ko <head> me add karke.
   Fir CSS me font-family use karte ho.
*/

/* 
    Specificity Order (highest → lowest)
   Inline Styles  >  ID Selector  >  Class/Attribute Selector  >  Element Selector  >  Universal Selector (*)
*/

/* 
    nth-child / first-child
   - Agar ek div me 5 <p> tags hain:
     → pehla p = first-child
     → doosra p = second-child
     → teesra p = third-child ... and so on.
   - nth-child(n) use karke tum kisi specific child ko target kar sakte ho.
*/
